  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T06:10:59.984Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nUnder Section 51 of the NIRC, the following individuals are required to file an individual income tax return: (1) every Filipino citizen residing in the Philippines; (2) every Filipino citizen residing outside the Philippines on income from sources within the Philippines; and (3) every alien residing in the Philippines on income derived from sources within the Philippines.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\n- **NIRC Section 51**: This section outlines the requirements for individuals to file income tax returns.\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 51 of the NIRC specifies that all Filipino citizens, regardless of their residency status, must file an income tax return if they have income from Philippine sources. Additionally, aliens who earn income from sources within the Philippines are also required to file. This provision ensures that both citizens and resident aliens contribute to the tax system based on their income sources.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThe requirement to file an income tax return under Section 51 emphasizes the obligation of individuals to report their income to the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR). This includes not only local residents but also citizens living abroad who earn income from the Philippines. Failure to comply with this requirement may result in penalties or legal consequences, highlighting the importance of understanding one's tax obligations based on residency and income sources.",
